{"author":"shoustak","children":[{"author":"shoustak","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-27T15:12:08.000Z","created_at_i":1790521928,"id":49867330,"options":[],"parent_id":49867329,"points":null,"story_id":49867329,"text":"Author here. Five 2026 studies, read side by side. The short version: a hand-written file helps a little (ETH v2: +2.4 points, not significant), a generated one comes out lower, both cost about 20% more. McMillan&#x27;s 1,650 Claude Code sessions found file size, rule position and layout made no detectable difference; compliance tended to fall as the session went on. Vercel&#x27;s docs index in AGENTS.md hit 100% where a skill left to the agent hit 53%. Every source is linked. I work on Harbor, which published it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-27T15:12:08.000Z","created_at_i":1790521928,"id":49867329,"options":[],"parent_id":null,"points":3,"story_id":49867329,"text":null,"title":"Is AGENTS.md useful? What the research found","type":"story","url":"https://gethrbr.com/blog/is-agents-md-useful"}
